// OStimAnchorAlign rules. Comments are allowed. Re-read at the start of every OStim scene.
//
// "bones":   anchor name -> list of skeleton node names; the first one that exists is used.
//            Anchors don't have to be exact contact points: the plugin keeps the relation the two
//            anchors would have at reference height, so the head works fine as "mouth".
// "actions": OStim action id (see SKSE/Plugins/OStim/actions) -> which anchor of the action
//            actor and of the action target should stay together, and how much this rule counts.
//            Set an action to null to disable it. Actions not listed here are ignored.
// "handTargets": hand target name -> bone groups. The first group with any bone present on the
//            skeleton is used; the hand goes to the nearest bone of that group.
// "handActions": OStim action id -> hand target. The action actor's nearest hand is bent (arm IK)
//            so it touches the target actor's part the way it would at reference height.
// "creatureBones" / "creatureHandTargets": same format as "bones" / "handTargets", tried first for
//            creature actors (built-in lists cover vanilla creature skeletons and BakaFactory / MNC
//            genital bones); creatureBones "fallback" is used when no other bone of an anchor exists.
// "creatureRaces": race editor ID substrings treated as creatures even with the ActorTypeNPC
//            keyword (default ["werewolf", "vampirebeast"]). Races without ActorTypeNPC always are.
// "replaceDefaults": true drops the built-in action and hand action lists, so only the ones below apply.
